The package kio provides CMake targets:

    find_package(KF6KIO CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE KF6::KIOCore KF6::KIOGui KF6::KIOWidgets)

    # Not available on Android
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE KF6::KIOFileWidgets)

KIO runs some operations in the helper executables kioworker and kioexec, which
it looks for next to the application and in PATH: applications using them must
deploy them from tools/kio next to their executable, or add tools/kio to PATH.
kioworker loads the worker plugins of the application, so debug builds of the
application must use the debug kioworker from debug/tools/kio instead.

On Linux and BSD, the password and SSL certificate services run in kiod6, which
the session bus starts through D-Bus service files. These are not installed,
since they need the absolute path of the deployed kiod6: applications using
these services must deploy kiod6 and install, in a directory searched by the
session bus, the service files org.kde.kiod6.service,
org.kde.kpasswdserver6.service, org.kde.kssld6.service and
org.kde.kioexecd6.service, each with its own Name:

    [D-BUS Service]
    Name=org.kde.kiod6
    Exec=/path/to/kiod6

On static triplets the protocol workers (file, http, ...) are not installed,
since KF6 only supports static plugins linked in the same build: every job
needing a worker fails, including local file operations.
